         <dc:format>application/pdf</dc:format>
         <photoshop:ColorMode>3</photoshop:ColorMode>
         <photoshop:ICCProfile>Generic RGB Profile</photoshop:ICCProfile>
         <photoshop:TextLayers>
            <rdf:Bag>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Generative AI in a Nutshell - how to survive and thrive in the </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Generative AI in a Nutshell - how to survive and thrive in the Age of AI  Welcome to the strange new world of Generative AI!  This book is a fast-paced, practical, and mostly human-written guide to what the heck is going on, and what you can do about it. It is like an extended version of Henrik's viral video with the same name.  This book covers questions like: What is generative AI? How does it work? How do I use it? What are some risks &amp; limitations? It also covers topics like how to lead an AI transformation, autonomous agents, the role of us humans, prompt engineering tips, AI-powered product development, different types of models, and some tips about mindset and how not to freak out.  Everything is explained in plain English with Henrik's signature hand-drawn illustrations and tons of concrete real-life examples. Minimum use of jargon and buzzwords.  Don't just survive the Age of AI ‚Äî learn how to thrive in it!    </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Henrik Kniberg is a cofounder and chief scientist at Ymnig.ai. </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Henrik Kniberg is a cofounder and chief scientist at Ymnig.ai. He is an AI whisperer, trainer, product developer, and author. Henrik is famous for his viral videos "Spotify Engineering Culture", "Product Ownership in a Nutshell", and "Generative AI in a Nutshell", for silly metaphors such as the skateboard metaphor for product development, and for his work as Minecraft developer. He lives in Stockholm with his wife and four kids and a bunch of random music instruments.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>"Henrik truly has a gift. He's able to quickly learn, and then </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>"Henrik truly has a gift. He's able to quickly learn, and then explain, nuanced and complex topics in ways that immediately resonate with people. And there is perhaps no more important subject to apply this talent than Generative AI. I hope you‚Äôll read this book, and share it with your colleagues." ‚Äî Marty Cagan, Founder, Silicon Valley Product Group  "It's great! What sets this book apart are three things: (1) not only good content, but it's presented informally and easy to understand; (2) the writing style‚ÄîI love it! Too much written about AI today is nearly unreadable; and (3) of course the wonderful, playful images"   ‚Äî Jim Highsmith, Co-author of the Agile Manifesto  "The beauty of this book is that Henrik is leading us along a path on which he is 2 steps ahead. Everyone will be affected by generative AI. The sooner we all begin steering the car instead of just being driven, the sooner we can regain a sense of agency. This book gives you the tools you need to overcome panic or inertia." ‚Äî Kent Beck - Software Development Pioneer, Creator of Extreme Programming  "I taught Henrik everything he knows about AI. Well, except for the parts he got wrong. Believe me, I could have written this entire book in a few seconds, but he wouldn't let me." ‚Äî Egbert</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Generative AI in a Nutshell</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Generative AI in a Nutshell</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Henrik Kniberg</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Henrik Kniberg</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Generative AI in a Nutshell</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Generative AI in a Nutshell</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>How to Survive and Thrive in the Age of AI</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>How to Survive and Thrive in the Age of AI</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Henrik Kniberg</photoshop:LayerName>
